      "items": [
        {
          "_id": "3JjOvltLmmBeqJD2aBZX5OndETq",
          "_index": "a0",
          "_type": "Question",
          "question": "Do I need a database?",
          "answer": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "Not for your content. It is stored as JSON files in your repository, and Alinea builds an SQLite index from those files for querying and search. With Alinea Cloud there is no database to run at all. If you "
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "self-host the backend",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "_type": "link",
                      "_id": "3JzmWGmWpG16BgxBcTPTkkYlsE3",
                      "_link": "entry",
                      "_entry": "2YlEGKqhO4mqRqEwQexeqRI8Jfu"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": ", you do need one for the dashboard's users and roles and for uploads until they are committed: PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQLite or PGlite."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_id": "3JjOvnlxcvQhbSinaRwFAsUjaWq",
          "_index": "a1",
          "_type": "Question",
          "question": "Does it work with the App Router and server components?",
          "answer": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "Yes. Alinea is built for the Next.js App Router. You query content directly in server components, and live previews render drafts on the server as editors type."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_id": "3JjOvm2HtCy914r68xZnvq6HWJm",
          "_index": "a2",
          "_type": "Question",
          "question": "Can I host it somewhere other than Vercel?",
          "answer": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "Yes. The dashboard ships with your Next.js app and deploys wherever Next.js runs. Run the backend yourself on your own database, or let Alinea Cloud handle sign-in and publishing."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_id": "3JjOvmz78vH2AXc6hsmHiKbjrTD",
          "_index": "a3",
          "_type": "Question",
          "question": "Do content edits trigger a rebuild?",
          "answer": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "They do not have to. Every publish is a git commit and your site picks up the new content without waiting for a build. Content-only commits can skip the rebuild, and static pages can be revalidated after each publish. See "
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "instant publishing",
                  "marks": [
